**W1-D1-Revision-Classes_and_Objects**

---

```
KEY POINTS:
- class = blueprint
- object = real thing built from blueprint
- __init__ = runs automatically when object created
- self = this specific object
- self.x = x = permanently store value on object
- method = function inside class
- return = sends value back (reusable)
- print = just displays, value gone after
- Django models/views/serializers = all classes
```

---

```python
# QUICK REFERENCE CODE

class Car:
    def __init__(self, brand, model, year):
        self.brand = brand
        self.model = model
        self.year = year

    def display_info(self):
        print(f"{self.year} {self.brand} {self.model}")

    def is_new(self):
        return self.year >= 2023

car1 = Car("Toyota", "Corolla", 2022)
car1.display_info()   # 2022 Toyota Corolla
print(car1.is_new())  # False
```

